+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Greenfield bootstrap complete
+
+- Project has one commit with spec assets and template.
+- Vanilla JS, no preprocessors, per user direction and app-spec.md.
+- localStorage key: `todos-vanillajs` (per TodoMVC convention for vanilla JS).
+- Two feature files authored: `features/todo-management.feature` and `features/todo-filtering.feature`.
+- Watchbill ordered in 8 watches: no-todos, create, complete/clear, delete, edit, counter, persistence, routing.
+
+## Open decisions
+
+- HTML template path: use `assets/app-template.index.html` as base, copy to `index.html`.
+- Directory structure per app-spec: `js/app.js`, `js/controllers/todos.js`, `js/models/todo.js`.
+- CSS: use `node_modules/todomvc-app-css/index.css` and `node_modules/todomvc-common/base.css`. Override in `css/app.css`.
+- Routing: use native hashchange (no Director library since it's vanilla JS and native routing suffices).
+- No test runner config needed yet — cucumber-js and happy-dom already installed.
+
+## Next steps
+
+1. QM reads durable artifacts from `features/` and `watchbill.json`, writes step definitions and support, dispatches Crew per failing target.
+2. Crew implements each watch's production code.
+3. Boatswain handles hygiene and local commit.
+4. After all watches green, report outbound options to user.
